From: Firmware Security Follow-up <security@local.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211 bound s1g tim payload

CVE: CVE-2026-74336
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/linus/b224d18b1e5d1cddfc67f63f41d80023b2ec8889]

S1G inline helpers remain in ieee80211.h before the upstream header split. The actual parser receives payload length excluding the two-byte element header.

--- a/include/linux/ieee80211.h
+++ b/include/linux/ieee80211.h
@@ -3109,7 +3109,7 @@
 	 */
 	err = ieee80211_s1g_find_target_block(&enc_blk, &target_aid,
 					      tim->virtual_map,
-					      (const u8 *)tim + tim_len + 2);
+					      (const u8 *)tim + tim_len);
 	if (err)
 		return false;
 
